 "notes": "Data from Wowhead Forever (patch 1.60.1), read 2026-11-16. Quest level, required level, side, start/end NPCs and coordinates come from each quest page's Quick Facts and map data. Coordinates are zone-map percentages (x,y) in the named zone.\nALCAZ PRISON = zone 16620 (entrance in the basement of the keep on north Alcaz Island, Dustwallow Marsh, zone 15). Wowhead files 15 quests under the dungeon category; I added the 6 breadcrumb/chain quests that lead there (95194, 95196, 95198, 95283, 95284, 95285) and Shaw Needs To Know 95264, giving 22 entries.\n- Quests started inside the dungeon: 96335 and 96337 from the prisoner Mason Connery (end of the dungeon), 95454 from Commander Folkar (260386, after Katerina), 96369 from a Perfumed Note after Blazeroar; 95263 and 95483 are return quests. Wowhead has no start NPC/object for these, so giver.id is null. Mason Connery has two NPC ids on Wowhead (264770, 264845) and neither is linked to a quest.\n- Event objectives: Wowhead ties 'Explore Alcaz Prison' / 'Find Varian Wrynn' to Blazeroar 255702, and 'Find Commander Folkar' to Katerina the Cleaner 257016. 'Learn what became of Varian' / 'Read the note on the ground' use credit id 264861 (a note in Zarla's room).\n- Sully McCleary has two ids: 260146 (Theramore inn, 66.2,45.2) and 260271 (behind the graveyard, 63.4,42.4). Most Alliance quests use 260271.\n- Sergeant Ulka: Wowhead quest map gives Dustwallow 70.3,19.1. The Wowhead guide's '/way 33.4 38' refers to a different map, so the 70.3,19.1 value matches Warcraft Tavern.\n- The Questioner (256236) is near the start of the dungeon; the toy guide says not to kill him until Mason Connery has given 96335.\n- State Secrets has 3 versions, all needing the Document Box (274041, the reward of 96337): 96376 Horde (Nazgrel, Orgrimmar), 96377 Alliance (Renzik, Stormwind), 96379 any faction (Rix Xizzix, Booty Bay). Each gives a Fractured Insignia (279450); six of them make the Alcaz Operative Disguise toy.\n- 95264 Shaw Needs To Know: starts at Sully 260271 and ends at Shaw. Wowhead lists no prerequisite; it probably follows Somber News 95263, but that is unconfirmed.\n- A Bit of Wet Work / A Little Payback / Blood Red Bandanas: the Wowhead guide marks them 'Pre' (they need the faction chain), but the quest pages do not give the exact prerequisite id.\nSHAPER'S TERRACE = zone 16667, but Wowhead's zone page is empty. Its NPCs are mapped to Kalimdor (location -6) and its quests sit in category 16985 ('Forever Zones'), so the dungeon 'Quests' tab shows nothing. I found all 6 quests by name, after Warcraft Tavern's guide listed them. Entrance per Warcraft Tavern: Un'Goro Crater 48.1,6.1, on the hill above Marshal's Refuge.\n- 95790 Digestible Research starts inside, at an abandoned camp in the pond below the entrance ledge (Warcraft Tavern). Wowhead has no start object/item, so giver is null and starts_from_item_inside is unknown (false by default).\n- The Crystalline Elements crystals (271912, 271898, 271902, 271894) and the Drained Crystal Fragment (271771) have no drop or object source on Wowhead yet. The Dark Crystal fragment is gathered next to the Achromatic Crystal (credit npc 263277) in the tar pits.\n- Dungeon mechanic, not a quest: 4 Archival Panels each take 15 Power Crystals of one colour (red summons Cinder, blue Snowtalon, green Vitrix, yellow Bolt). After all four, the Titan Panel on the Pillar of Assimilation summons Nanaya.\n- Left out on purpose: 87492 Uncanny Crystal and 87494 Microcrystal Contamination (Torwa Pathfinder, open-world Un'Goro, item from regular Un'Goro mobs) and 94399 Ravasaur Provisions. They are new Forever Un'Goro quests but are not tied to the dungeon. Retail quest 24694 'The Shaper's Terrace' does not exist in Forever.\nRUSSIAN NAMES: on Wowhead ru (www.wowhead.com/forever/ru/quest=ID) the new quest titles and texts are still in English (shown in [brackets]), so name_ru is null for every quest. Item names are translated (e.g. 271771 = 'Опустошенный осколок кристалла').\nNot found: Shaper's Terrace boss order (bosses can be done in any order); exact drop sources for the 5 crystals; Mason Connery's exact NPC id; start objects for 96369 and 95790.",
